WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.408
Hi! Today we talk about yesterday.

2
00:00:06.808 --> 00:00:11.064
You learn the perfect tense: what did you do?

3
00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:18.511
In German we talk about the past with haben and a participle:

4
00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:21.631
I ate pizza.

5
00:00:22.031 --> 00:00:27.223
Haben is in position two, the participle at the end:

6
00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:30.535
We listened to music.

7
00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:36.921
Regular verbs: ge plus stem plus t:

8
00:00:37.321 --> 00:00:40.113
make, made

9
00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:43.425
buy, bought

10
00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:47.073
play, played

11
00:00:47.473 --> 00:00:50.769
work, worked

12
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:58.475
Many important verbs end in en. Learn them like vocabulary:

13
00:00:58.875 --> 00:01:01.571
eat, eaten

14
00:01:01.971 --> 00:01:05.171
drink, drunk

15
00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:08.339
see, seen

16
00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:11.699
read, read

17
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.264
Listen: it's Monday. Lena asks Mateo.

18
00:01:19.664 --> 00:01:22.984
What did you do?

19
00:01:23.384 --> 00:01:26.272
I played football.

20
00:01:26.672 --> 00:01:29.152
And I cooked.

21
00:01:29.552 --> 00:01:32.104
What did you cook?

22
00:01:32.504 --> 00:01:36.208
A soup. And you?

23
00:01:36.608 --> 00:01:39.424
I read a lot.

24
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:48.557
Now you! What did you do yesterday? Say three sentences with habe.

25
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:04.403
Great! Now you can:

26
00:02:04.803 --> 00:02:10.355
You say what you did – with haben and the participle.

27
00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:12.875
See you soon!
